@startuml EMREX_iGov_Compliant_Flow_Details
autonumber "<b>[000]"

title **EMREX Flow - OpenID iGov Compliant met Gedetailleerde Authorization Request**

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor "Student Browser" as browser
participant "EMC Frontend" as emc_fe
participant "EMC Backend" as emc_bff
participant "EMP Frontend" as emp_fe
participant "EMP Backend" as emp_bff
participant "EMP Resource Server" as emp_rs
participant "EMREG" as emreg

== 1. Institution Selection ==
browser -> emc_fe: Start transfer
emc_fe -> emc_bff: Get available EMPs
emc_bff -> emreg: GET /emp-list
emreg --> emc_bff: EMP metadata (iGov 4.1.1)
emc_bff --> emc_fe: EMP options
emc_fe --> browser: Show EMP selection

== 2. Authorization Request Preparation ==
browser -> emc_fe: Select EMP
emc_fe -> emc_bff: Prepare auth request

group **PKCE + JWT Preparation (iGov 5.2)**
  emc_bff -> emc_bff: code_verifier = BASE64URL(SHA256(random(32)))\ncode_challenge = BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))
  emc_bff -> emc_bff: Generate JWT with:\n- Header: alg=RS256, typ=JWT, kid=EMC_KEY_ID\n- Payload: iss, sub, aud, jti, iat, exp, nbf, azp (iGov 5.6.2)
end group

group **Detailed Authorization Request Construction (Stap 10)**
  note right: **Base URL**: EMP Authorization Endpoint (bijv. https://emp.sweden.edu/authorize)
  note right: **Verplichte Parameters (iGov 5.1):**
  note right: **1. response_type=code**
  note right:   - Waarde: "code"
  note right:   - Doel: Specificeert authorization code flow
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1

  note right: **2. client_id=EMC_CLIENT_ID**
  note right:   - Waarde: "emc-nl-university1" (voorbeeld)
  note right:   - Doel: Identificeert EMC bij EMP
  note right:   - Validatie: Moet geregistreerd zijn in EMREG
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1.1

  note right: **3. redirect_uri=EMC_CALLBACK_URL**
  note right:   - Waarde: "https://emc.university.nl/callback" (voorbeeld)
  note right:   - Doel: Callback URL voor EMC
  note right:   - Validatie: Moet exact matchen met geregistreerde URI in EMREG
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1.2

  note right: **4. scope=openid elmo**
  note right:   - Waarde: "openid elmo" (of "openid elmo profile")
  note right:   - Doel:
  note right:     - openid: OIDC conformiteit
  note right:     - elmo: EMREX resultaten
  note right:     - profile: Optioneel voor persoonsgegevens
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1.3

  note right: **5. state=CSRF_TOKEN**
  note right:   - Waarde: "xYz123abc456def789" (voorbeeld)
  note right:   - Doel: CSRF bescherming
  note right:   - Eigenschappen:
  note right:     - Uniek per sessie
  note right:     - Minimaal 16 karakters
  note right:     - Willekeurige string
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1.4

  note right: **6. nonce=NONCE_VALUE**
  note right:   - Waarde: "nOnCe1234567890" (voorbeeld)
  note right:   - Doel: Replay attack bescherming
  note right:   - Eigenschappen:
  note right:     - Uniek per request
  note right:     - Minimaal 16 karakters
  note right:     - Wordt teruggegeven in ID Token
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.1.5

  note right: **7. code_challenge=CODE_CHALLENGE**
  note right:   - Waarde: BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))
  note right:   - Doel: PKCE bescherming
  note right:   - Voorbeeld:
  note right:     - code_verifier = "xYz123...789" (43-128 karakters)
  note right:     - code_challenge = BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.2

  note right: **8. code_challenge_method=S256**
  note right:   - Waarde: "S256"
  note right:   - Doel: Specificeert PKCE methode
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.2

  note right: **9. client_assertion_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer**
  note right:   - Waarde: "urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer"
  note right:   - Doel: Specificeert JWT assertie type
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.5

  note right: **10. client_assertion=GENERATED_JWT**
  note right:   - Waarde: JWT met RS256 signature
  note right:   - JWT structuur:
  note right:     Header: {alg: "RS256", typ: "JWT", kid: "EMC_KEY_ID"}
  note right:     Payload: {iss: "EMC_CLIENT_ID", sub: "EMC_CLIENT_ID", aud: "EMP_TOKEN_URL",
  note right:     jti: "UNIQUE_ID", iat: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, exp: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP+300,
  note right:     nbf: CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, azp: "EMC_CLIENT_ID"}
  note right:   - Referentie: iGov 5.6.2

  note right: **Optionele parameters:**
  note right:   - prompt=consent (expliciete toestemming)
  note right:   - max_age=3600 (sessie levensduur)
  note right:   - ui_locales=nl-NL (lokalisatie)

  note right: **Voorbeeld URL (ge-encode):**
  note right: https://emp.sweden.edu/authorize?
  note right: response_type=code&
  note right: client_id=emc-nl-university1&
  note right: redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Femc.university.nl%2Fcallback&
  note right: scope=openid%20elmo&
  note right: state=xYz123abc456def789&
  note right: nonce=nOnCe1234567890&
  note right: code_challenge=E9Melv6jU2FjOq4A2TesOYsX9jpwcKQV86Z5HnXKhtI&
  note right: code_challenge_method=S256&
  note right: client_assertion_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Aclient-assertion-type%3Ajwt-bearer&
  note right: client_assertion=eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6IkVNQ19LRVlfSUQifQ...

  note right: **Validatieregels:**
  note right: 1. Alle verplichte parameters aanwezig
  note right: 2. JWT correct ondertekend met EMC private key
  note right: 3. JWT claims valide (iss==client_id, aud==EMP_token_URL, etc.)
  note right: 4. redirect_uri moet exact matchen met geregistreerde URI in EMREG
  note right: 5. scope bevat minimaal "openid"
  note right: 6. code_challenge correct gegenereerd (S256 van code_verifier)
  note right: 7. state en nonce uniek per request
end group

emc_bff --> emc_fe: Authorization parameters
emc_fe --> browser: Redirect to EMP with complete authorization request

== 3. EMP Client Verification (iGov 5.6) ==
browser -> emp_fe: GET /authorize with parameters
emp_fe -> emreg: GET /clients/EMC_CLIENT_ID\nAuthorization: Bearer EMP_API_TOKEN
emreg --> emp_fe: Client metadata with public key

group **JWT Validation (iGov 5.6.3)**
  emp_fe -> emp_fe: Verify signature with EMC public key
  emp_fe -> emp_fe: Validate claims (iss, aud, exp, nbf, azp)
end group

alt JWT valid
    emp_fe -> browser: Show login form
else JWT invalid
    emp_fe --> browser: Redirect to EMC with:\nerror=invalid_client\nerror_description=JWT+verification+failed\nstate=ORIGINAL_STATE (iGov 5.7)
end

== 4. User Authentication & Consent ==
browser -> emp_fe: Submit credentials
emp_fe -> emp_bff: Validate user (iGov 6.1)
emp_bff -> emp_bff: Get student results
emp_bff --> emp_fe: Results for selection
emp_fe --> browser: Show results selection

browser -> emp_fe: Select results + consent
emp_fe -> emp_rs: Store user selection (ref_id=UUID, selected_results)
emp_rs --> emp_fe: Confirm storage

group **Authorization Code Generation (iGov 6.2)**
  emp_fe -> emp_bff: Generate auth code
  emp_bff -> emp_bff: Bind code to user selection
  emp_bff --> emp_fe: Auth code
end group

emp_fe --> browser: Redirect to EMC with:\ncode=AUTH_CODE\nstate=CSRF_TOKEN (iGov 6.3)

== 5. Token Exchange (iGov 7) ==
browser -> emc_fe: Return with auth code
emc_fe -> emc_bff: Forward auth code + code_verifier

group **Token Request (iGov 7.1)**
  emc_bff -> emp_bff: POST /token with:\ngrant_type=authorization_code\ncode=AUTH_CODE\nredirect_uri=EMC_CALLBACK_URL\ncode_verifier=CODE_VERIFIER\nclient_assertion_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer\nclient_assertion=NEW_JWT
end group

emp_bff -> emreg: GET /clients/EMC_CLIENT_ID\nAuthorization: Bearer EMP_API_TOKEN
emreg --> emp_bff: Client metadata with public key

group **Token Validation (iGov 7.2)**
  emp_bff -> emp_bff: Verify JWT signature
  emp_bff -> emp_bff: Validate code_verifier
  emp_bff -> emp_bff: Generate tokens
end group

emp_bff --> emc_bff: Access token + ID token (iGov 7.3)

== 6. Data Retrieval with Signed Responses ==
group **ELMO XML (iGov 8.1)**
  emc_bff -> emp_rs: GET /results/elmo\nAuthorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
  emp_rs -> emp_rs: Sign response with EMP private key (iGov 8.2)
  emp_rs --> emc_bff: Signed ELMO XML\nX-Signature: EMP_SIGNATURE\nX-Signature-Algorithm: RS256\nX-Certificate-Thumbprint: EMP_CERT_THUMBPRINT
end group

group **PDF Document**
  emc_bff -> emp_rs: GET /results/pdf\nAuthorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
  emp_rs -> emp_rs: Sign response with EMP private key
  emp_rs --> emc_bff: PDF document\nX-Signature: EMP_SIGNATURE\nX-Signature-Algorithm: RS256\nX-Certificate-Thumbprint: EMP_CERT_THUMBPRINT
end group

group **ELM JSON**
  emc_bff -> emp_rs: GET /results/elm\nAuthorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
  emp_rs -> emp_rs: Sign response with EMP private key
  emp_rs --> emc_bff: ELM JSON\nX-Signature: EMP_SIGNATURE\nX-Signature-Algorithm: RS256\nX-Certificate-Thumbprint: EMP_CERT_THUMBPRINT
end group

== 7. Optional User Information (iGov 9) ==
emc_bff -> emp_rs: GET /userinfo\nAuthorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
alt userinfo enabled
    emp_rs --> emc_bff: User information (iGov 9.1)\n{\n  "sub": "user123",\n  "given_name": "John",\n  "family_name": "Doe",\n  "birthdate": "1990-01-01"\n}
else userinfo disabled
    emp_rs --> emc_bff: 403 Forbidden\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_scope"
end

@enduml